g Delete a Tag Webhook Webhook API overview List all Webhooks Retrieve a Webhook Create a Webhook Update a Webhook Delete a Webhook Company Company overview Retrieve Company information Integration Integration overview Retrieve Integration information Enable Integration Disable Integration Participant Participant overview IVR Option IVR Option overview AI Voice Agent AI Voice Agent overview Call AI Voice Agents Call AI Voice Agents overview Trigger an Outbound Call Template Variables Event Statuses Analytics Analytics overview Create an Analytics Report Export Retrieve an Analytics Report Export Webhooks Register an endpoint Webhook usage Payload User events V1 user.created user.deleted user.connected user.disconnected user.opened user.closed user.wut_start user.wut_end User events V2 user.created.v2 user.deleted.v2 user.connected.v2 user.disconnected.v2 user.opened.v2 user.closed.v2 user.wut_start.v2 user.wut_end.v2 Call events call.created call.ringing_on_agent call.agent_declined call.answered call.transferred call.external_transferred call.unsuccessful_transfer call.hungup call.ended call.voicemail_left call.commented call.tagged call.untagged call.assigned call.archived call.hold call.unhold call.ivr_option_selected call.comm_assets_generated Conversation events conversation.closed conversation.created conversation.reopened conversation.assigned Number events number.created number.deleted number.opened number.closed Message events message.sent message.received message.status_updated WhatsApp username message whatsapp_username_message.sent whatsapp_username_message.received whatsapp_username_message.status_updated group_message.sent group_message.received group_message.status_updated Contact events contact.created contact.updated contact.deleted Integration events integration.deleted Conversation Intelligence events sentiment.created summary.created topics.created transcription.created action_item.created playbook_result.created playbook_result.updated realtime_transcription.utterances_received custom_summary.result_created custom_summary.result_updated call_evaluation.created call_evaluation.updated AI Voice Agent events ai_voice_agent.started ai_voice_agent.ended ai_voice_agent.escalated ai_voice_agent.summary Analytics events analytics.report_created analytics.report_failed Outbound Campaign events outbound_campaign.outcome_recorded outbound_campaign.status_changed AI Messaging Agent events ai_messaging_agent.escalated ai_messaging_agent.de_escalated Mobile URL Schemes Open app (iOS) Call (Android & iOS) Changelog Extras CTI - Aircall Everywhere SDK Dealing with phone numbers SIP trunking Timezones Emojis Just like you, we are enthusiastic builders and we love to automate things. At Aircall, we are building the next-gen business phone system and we know that one of the best ways to do that is to give you the ability to have the hands on Aircall features. We are maintaining a Public API . This service allows any developers to retrieve and manage Aircall data with HTTP requests. We are also supporting Webhooks . We can call back any endpoint of your choice, each time an event occurs on an Aircall account (contact added, call created, user switched off... see the Webhooks section for a complete list). Webhooks provide great scalability to your application and only requires setting up a public web server! Want to see an example of how easy it is to connect with Aircall Public API and Webhooks? Take a look at our tutorials ! Our Engineering team is on Twitter, follow them @aircalltech ! Check the Changelog if you've already implemented something based on previous versions of this documentation. By visiting or using this developers website, you agree to be bound by Aircallâs API License Agreement Not a Developer? Install one of many integrations built by our partners in our Marketplace ! Ã as Ã Confirm Subscribe to updates Please subscribe to stay updated with the latest API and webhook updates. Subscribe By submitting the information, you confirm that you have read and acknowledged Aircall's Privacy Policy. Â REST API Aircall Public API is a classic REST API. It can be used with any programming languages and offers a fast, reliable and secure access to an Aircall account information. The root endpoint of Aircall Public API is https://api.aircall.io/v1 . Please note that only HTTPS requests are valid as requests will communicate over SSL connection. Each Public API request must be authenticated and should not exceed the rate limit, please check the Authentication and the rate limiting sections before jumping in our documentation! Request GET https://api.aircall.io Response {
  "resource": "Aircall Documentation",
  "contact": "support@aircall.io"
} Authentication Introduction With Aircall Public API, Authentication can be done through OAuth or Basic Auth. If you want to build an App for companies using Aircall - this is mainly the case for Technology Partners - please use the OAuth flow . It is a requirement to be listed on the Aircall App Marketplace. You can create a partner-specific account by signing up here ! If you are an Aircall customer, building for your own Aircall account only, the Basic Auth flow will do the trick. All endpoints behave similarly between the two authentication methods, unless indicated otherwise in the documentation. OAuth ï¹£ Technology Partners Aircall built a powerful Ecosystem of apps, providing its customers an easy way to enhance their voice experience. In Aircall, integrations are enabled at the Company level, which means they can only be set by an Admin user. It is possible to configure several instances of an integration on one Aircall account. Aircall implemented the OAuth 2.0 authentication protocol so you can easily build an app on top of Aircall and deploy it on Aircall's Marketplace. Beyond the added security and scalability, the Aircall OAuth flow will make your app visible to all customers in the Aircall Dashboard and provide a simple way for customers to install your app from Aircall or from your own website. Want to know every secret about OAuth? Read the official documentation RFC 6750 ! Oauth terminology install_uri String Aircall fetches the install_uri URI when starting the OAuth flow. This step is often used to display a Settings page, instructions on how to use the app or any useful information for the Admin. It must eventually forward to https://dashboard.aircall.io/oauth/authorize with client_id , redirect_uri , response_type=code and scope=public_api query params. See Step 3 of the OAuth flow . Must use HTTPS . redirect_uri String Aircall sends the Admin's authorization code to the redirect_uri URI, once they authorized the app, or the error if any. Must use HTTPS . client_id String Used in both the [DASHBOARD] /oauth/authorize and [API] /v1/oauth/token request. Provided by Aircall. client_secret String Used in the request body of [API] /v1/oauth/token . Provided by Aircall. code String An authentication code provided by Aircall valid for 10min. Must be converted in an access_token (see this endpoint ). access_token String Token used to send requests to Aircall Public API as a Company . More info on how to use it here . state String An optional string value created by your app to maintain state between the request and callback. This parameter should be used for preventing Cross-site Request Forgery and will be passed back to you, unchanged, in your redirect_uri . OAuth credentials Before starting building the OAuth flow for your app, you will need to get OAuth client_id and client_secret from Aircall. Click the start building button on top of the page and fill in the form. We will get back to you shortly. When signing up, an install_uri and a redirect_uri will be asked, make sure you have them ready. Read the OAuth flow first to understand what they are! OAuth flow Aircall ï¹£ When an Admin installs an App, a popup opens up and loads the install_uri URL. Partner ï¹£ A Web server receives the GET request on the install_uri route. This step is often used to display a custom Settings page, instructions on how to use the app and/or any useful information for the Admin. Partner ï¹£ Once Step 2 is done, Web server redirects/forwards the request to the following Aircall URL: https://dashboard.aircall.io/oauth/authorize?client_id=XX&redirect_uri=YY&response_type=code&scope=public_api&state=ZZ Aircall ï¹£ Aircall then displays the authorization window. Only users who are Admins will be able to see this window, others will be redirected to the Download page. Once the Admin consented to the permissions the app is requesting ( scope=public_api ), Aircall loads the redirect_uri URL with a code parameter. Partner ï¹£ Web server receives the GET request on the redirect_uri route with the code query paramâ¦ Partner ï¹£ â¦and sends a [POST] https://api.aircall.io/v1/oauth/token request to Aircall's Public API with the proper body params (see here ). Aircall ï¹£ Aircall authenticates the [POST] request, create an access_token and sends it back to the Web server. Partner ï¹£ Web server stores the access_token for further use! Start the instructions at Step 3 if you want to trigger the install flow directly from your interface and not from the Aircall Dashboard. Integrations can only be installed by users who are Admins on Aircall! Check out our Ruby example app on Github to better understand how to implement the Aircall OAuth flow! Get an access_token via the Public API Once you get an OAuth authorization code from the OAuth flow, you need to convert it into a Public API access_token with the following request. This access_token will then be used as a Bearer token in the Authorization header of each Public API requests you will make and does not expire. Body params client_id String The client_id provided by Aircall. More information in the Oauth credentials section. Mandatory field. client_secret String The client_secret provided by Aircall. More information in the Oauth credentials section. Mandatory field. code String The OAuth authorization code Aircall sent back to your server. Mandatory field. redirect_uri String Your redirect_uri . Mandatory field. grant_type String Must be authorization_code . Mandatory field. Request POST https://api.aircall.io/v1/oauth/token
{
  "client_id": YOUR_AIRCALL_CLIENT_ID,
  "client_secret": YOUR_AIRCALL_CLIENT_SECRET,
  "code": TMP_AUTHORIZATION_CODE,
  "redirect_uri": YOUR_REDIRECT_URI,
  "grant_type": "authorization_code"
} Response Status: 200 OK

{
  "access_token": "2d492d492d492d492d492d492d492d",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "created_at": 1585868617
} Test the access_token A /v1/ping endpoint is available to test the access_token retrieved via the Public API (as described here ). The access_token must be used in the Authorization HTTP header of your request, as a Bearer token . Request curl -X GET https://api.aircall.io/v1/ping \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" Response Status: 200 OK

{
  "ping": "pong"
} Basic Auth ï¹£ Aircall customers As an Aircall customer, an api_id and api_token are needed to use Aircall Public API: go to your Company's Settings page . In the API Keys section, click on Add a new API key and get your api_token and api_token . Do not forget to copy/paste your api_token somewhere safe, we won't be able to retrieve it for you as Aircall does not store it in plain text! If you are building an App for several companies using Aircall, please refer to the OAuth section . Public API requests must be authenticated using HTTP Basic Authentication . The api_id is the username and the api_token is the password for each Public API requests. The Authorization HTTP header is constructed as follows: The api_id and api_token are concatenated with a single colon : . The resulting string is encoded using Base64. The authorization header results in Authorization: Basic YOUR_ENCODED_STRING . Always prefer Base64 encoding in the Authorization HTTP header rather than the following: https://api_id:api_token@api.aircall.io . It is not recommended to authenticate requests passing the api_id and api_token in the URL for security reasons and as some programming languages and platforms do not support it! Request curl -X GET https://api.aircall.io/v1/ping \
     -H "Authorization: Basic {YOUR_ENCODED_STRING}" Response Status: 200 OK

{
  "ping": "pong"
} Rate limiting Aircall limits the number of requests to its Public API to 120 requests per minute per company. The following headers are available in API headers' responses when the rate limit has been reached, giving more insight on your API usage: header description X-AircallApi-Limit Limit of requests for the API key used. X-AircallApi-Remaining Remaining requests for this API key. X-AircallApi-Reset Timestamp when the counter will be reset. Contact us on support.aircall.io if you need to make more requests per minute, we will add a higher rate limit to your API keys! Pagination When retrieving a list of objects with a [GET] request, results are being paginated by Aircall. Pagination information will be presented in the meta object, available in the payload body and described below. The meta object count Integer Count of items present in the current page. total Integer Count of items in total, according to search params. current_page Integer Current page number. per_page Integer Number of results retrieved per page. Default is 20 . Minimum is 1 , maximum is 50 . next_page_link String URL to follow to go to the next page results. Can be null . previous_page_link String URL to follow to go to the previous page results. Can be null . The two following attributes can be set in any URL query params to navigate from one page to the other: Query params page Integer Current page. Default is 1 . per_page Integer Number of results retrieved per page Default is 20 . Calls and Contacts are limited to 10,000 items, even with pagination on.
  To pass over this limit, we encourage you to use the from param as much as you can! Response {
  "meta": {
    "count": 20,
    "total": 2234,
    "current_page": 1,
    "per_page": 20,
    "next_page_link": "https://api.aircall.io/v1/calls?page=2&per_page=20",
    "previous_page_link": null
  },
  ...
} Errors Aircall uses standard HTTP response codes to indicate the success or failure of an API request: 2xx codes indicate success 4xx codes indicate an error that failed given the information provided 5xx codes indicate an error with Aircall's servers Application error responses include an error title and a human-readable troubleshoot description. They also include message , an errors array, and success: false . Requests rejected at the API gateway before they reach an application, such as invalid credentials, can return a shorter gateway error. The Conversation endpoints return only error and troubleshoot . For Outbound Campaigns, message is the machine-readable code to use for specific handling. A recognised domain error uses a semantic code such as INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION or OUTCOME_IN_USE ; otherwise it falls back to the HTTP status constant such as BAD_REQUEST or UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY . errors[].detail always keeps that status-level constant for broad HTTP categorisation. Internal shared-library codes, including numeric codes, are never exposed. More detailed HTTP response codes are provided in each endpoint's documentation. Response {
  "error": "Unprocessable Entity",
  "message": "INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION",
  "errors": [
    {
      "status": 422,
      "title": "Unprocessable Entity",
      "detail": "UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY"
    }
  ],
  "troubleshoot": "Cannot transition campaign from \"completed\" to \"in_progress\"",
  "success": false
} code description 200 OK - The request has succeeded. 201 Created - The request has been fulfilled and has resulted in one or more new resources being created. 204 No Content - Server has successfully fulfilled the request, no additional content sent in the response payload body. 400 Bad Request - Server cannot process the request due to something that is perceived to be a client error. 403 Forbidden - Lack of valid authentication credentials for the target resource. 404 Not Found - Server did not find the target resource. 405 Method Not Allowed - The method is known by the server but not supported. 409 Conflict - The resource changed concurrently or otherwise conflicts with the requested operation. 413 Payload Too Large - The request exceeds the allowed payload size. 415 Unsupported Media Type - The request uses an unsupported content type. 422 Unprocessable Entity - The request is valid, but the resource's current state does not allow the operation. 429 Too Many Requests - The request exceeded a rate limit. 500 Internal Server Error - Server encountered an unexpected condition. 503 Service Unavailable - A required service is temporarily unavailable. Versioning Versioning Strategy Aircall APIs and Webhooks are versioned to allow for continuous evolution and improvement while maintaining backward compatibility for existing integrations. API versions are indicated in the URL path. The webhook event names are now suffixed with âv2â. For APIs, Aircall uses URL-based versioning, where the API version is included directly in the endpoint path. For example: Version 1 endpoints: /v1/users , /v1/calls , etc. Version 2 endpoints: /v2/users , etc. For Webhook events, the version number is suffixed in the event name. For example: Version 1 webhook event: user.connected Version 2 webhook event: user.connected.v2 As of now, v2 of user APIs and webhook events is available Content-Type Every POST , PUT and DELETE HTTP request sent to Aircall Public API  must specify the Content-Type entity header to application/json . Request HTTP headers:
{ "Content-Type": "application/json" } Announcements Please refer to this section for announcements related to deprecation or changes as well as availability of new APIs and Webhooks. Title Description Changes effective from Impacted/New Endpoints Deprecation/Last Change Date Campaign contact import now imports directly Loading a CSV file of contacts into a Campaign no longer has a review step: once the file is uploaded, its valid rows become Campaign contacts and join the dial queue as it is read. The create request takes insertion_point ( start / end , default start ), the import status values are pending , processing , imported , failed and stopped , and Retrieve a Campaign contact import carries the whole import summary. POST /v1/campaigns/:id/contact_imports/:import_id/promote and GET /v1/campaigns/:id/contact_imports/:import_id/rows are removed: nothing is staged for review, and an import keeps counts rather than per-row records. 04-11-2026 Create a Campaign contact import Retrieve a Campaign contact import POST /v1/campaigns/:id/contact_imports/:import_id/promote (removed) GET /v1/campaigns/:id/contact_imports/:import_id/rows (removed) 04-11-2026 New Conversation endpoints and webhook events Six new endpoints are available to find, read, close, reopen and assign Conversations : GET /v1/conversations - List all Conversations. GET /v1/conversations/:id - Retrieve a Conversation. GET /v1/conversations/:id/engagements - List the Engagements of a Conversation. POST /v1/conversations/:id/close - Close a Conversation. POST /v1/conversations/:id/reopen - Reopen a Conversation. POST /v1/conversations/:id/assign - Assign a Conversation. Four new Webhook events are available for subscription: conversation.closed , conversation.created , conversation.reopened and conversation.assigned .
      The Conversation endpoints and webhook events are only available to companies for which they have been enabled. Other companies can subscribe to the events, but receive none until then. 30-10-2026 List all Conversations Retrieve a Conversation List the Engagements of a Conversation Close a Conversation Reopen a Conversation Assign a Conversation conversation.closed conversation.created conversation.reopened conversation.assigned N/A New WhatsApp username message webhook events Three new webhook events describe sent messages, received messages, and delivery status updates for WhatsApp conversations identified by a BSUID.
      These events are available for subscription. See WhatsApp username message for payload fields and routing behavior. 13-10-2026 whatsapp_username_message.sent whatsapp_username_message.received whatsapp_username_message.status_updated N/A New AI Messaging Agent webhook events Two new Webhook events for AI Messaging Agent: ai_messaging_agent.escalated and ai_messaging_agent.de_escalated . Subscribe to know when a conversation needs a human teammate's attention and when that escalation has been resolved. 30-09-2026 ai_messaging_agent.escalated ai_messaging_agent.de_escalated N/A New Outbound Campaign Webhook events Two new Webhook events for Campaigns: outbound_campaign.outcome_recorded and outbound_campaign.status_changed . Subscribe to react to campaign lifecycle changes and call outcomes without polling. 17-09-2026 outbound_campaign.outcome_recorded outbound_campaign.status_changed N/A New Conversation Intelligence - Trackers Endpoints Two new endpoints are available to use Conversation Trackers capabilities via API: GET /v1/trackers - List all Trackers configured for your company. GET /v1/trackers/:tracker_id - Retrieve a Tracker and the calls currently matching its filters. Requires the AI Assist or AI Assist Pro package. 08-09-2026 List all Trackers Retrieve a Tracker N/A New Campaigns API Outbound Campaigns are now available via the public API: Retrieve a Campaign , List all Campaigns , Retrieve Campaign statistics , and List Campaign call outcomes . An API token has company-wide access to Campaigns. See Outbound Campaigns for details. 17-09-2026 Retrieve a Campaign List all Campaigns Retrieve Campaign statistics List Campaign call outcomes N/A New Campaigns API - lifecycle, assignment and outcome recording The Campaigns public API now supports creating, editing, deleting and moving a Campaign through its lifecycle (launch/pause/resume/archive), assigning Users and Teams to it, recording call outcomes, and reading its resolved agent ring, caller-id pool, contacts and dial queue. Launch requires a compliance acknowledgment that the caller has the right to dial the Campaign's contacts. Archive is irreversible, and a completed Campaign can only move to archived. See the Outbound Campaigns section for details. 17-09-2026 Create a Campaign Update a Campaign Delete a Campaign Launch a Campaign Pause a Campaign Resume a Campaign Archive a Campaign Record a Campaign call outcome List Campaign users Assign users to a Campaign Remove a user from a Campaign List Campaign teams Assign teams to a Campaign Remove a team from a Campaign List Campaign agents List Campaign lines List Campaign contacts List Campaign queue items N/A New Campaign Outcomes API A new company-wide catalogue of custom call outcomes for Campaigns is now available via the public API: create, retrieve, list, update and delete a Campaign Outcome . This is the referent behind the outcome.id a custom outcome carries on List Campaign call outcomes . 17-09-2026 List all Campaign Outcomes Create a Campaign Outcome Retrieve a Campaign Outcome Update a Campaign Outcome Delete a Campaign Outcome N/A New Campaign Eligible Numbers API Discover which of your company's numbers are allowed as a Campaign caller ID via List Campaign eligible numbers - company-wide and Campaign-agnostic, the same access model as Campaign Outcome . Only numbers that pass outbound dialling compliance rules are returned. 17-09-2026 List Campaign eligible numbers N/A New Duplicate Campaign endpoint Copy a Campaign's settings - name, retry policy, caller-ID strategy, assigned outcome catalogue, caller ID numbers, and User/Team assignment - into a new draft Campaign via Duplicate a Campaign . Contacts are not copied. 17-09-2026 Duplicate a Campaign N/A New Campaign queue management endpoints Move a Campaign queue entry to the top/bottom or past a neighbour with Reorder a Campaign queue item , or defer/clear when it's due with Reschedule a Campaign queue item . Both endpoints require the queue entry to belong to the Campaign in the path; a wrong or nonexistent Campaign id returns 404 . 17-09-2026 Reorder a Campaign queue item Reschedule a Campaign queue item N/A AI Voice Agent Campaigns and Caller ID pools on the Campaigns API The new AIVA campaigns guide connects the creation, contact and launch rules for this Campaign variant. Create a Campaign accepts caller_id_numbers , so a Campaign using caller_id_strategy: "specific_number_pool" can be created with its Caller ID pool and launched in the same flow. Pick the numbers from List Campaign eligible numbers . The same endpoint also creates AI Voice Agent Campaigns, via agent_type , aiva_agent_id and calling_hours , and the Campaign object now reports all three so you can tell the two kinds apart. Update a Campaign accepts caller_id_numbers and calling_hours . Each agent type is a separate per-company entitlement. 17-09-2026 AIVA campaigns Create a Campaign Update a Campaign Campaign N/A New synchronous Campaign contacts API Add 1-100 contacts to a Campaign and queue them for dialling in a single request, without the CSV upload round trip: Add Campaign contacts . Results align positionally with the request and carry a status plus a rejection reason when applicable. A 201 means at least one contact was queued; a 200 can mean every contact was rejected. Neither successful response has a success key. For larger volumes, continue to use the Campaign contact import flow. The matching undo is Remove a Campaign contact , which takes one contact back out of the dial queue. A contact with no recorded attempts is deleted outright; a contact that has already been called leaves the queue, has its remaining retries cancelled, and keeps its latest known outcome when one exists. 17-09-2026 Add Campaign contacts Remove a Campaign contact N/A New Campaign contact import API Load a CSV file of contacts into a Campaign: create an import and get a presigned upload target, poll its status , inspect per-row validation results, then promote the valid rows into the dial queue (per-row results and the promote step were removed on 04-11-2026 - see the announcement above). For AIVA Campaigns, ordered field_mapping.variables pairs map CSV columns to every required agent context variable; see the worked example . 17-09-2026 Create a Campaign contact import Retrieve a Campaign contact import N/A New Conversation Intelligence - Predicted CSAT Endpoint Retrieve Predicted CSAT - Fetch Predicted CSAT score and drivers for a call via API. 06-07-2026 Retrieve Predicted CSAT N/A New Analytics Webhook Events Two new webhook events let you be notified when an Analytics report export finishes, removing the need to poll the retrieve endpoint: analytics.report_created â Fired when an export job completes successfully. Payload includes the presigned download_url and its expiry. analytics.report_failed â Fired when an export job fails. Payload includes error_code and error_message . Pair with Create an Analytics Report Export to drop polling entirely. 26-05-2026 analytics.report_created analytics.report_failed N/A New Analytics Report Export Endpoints Two new endpoints expose Aircall's analytics report exports via the public API. Reports are generated asynchronously: create an export job, poll for status, then download the CSV from a presigned URL. Create an Analytics Report Export â Submit an asynchronous export job for one of 12 supported report types (CALLS_HISTORY, USER_STATUS_HISTORY, and ten USER_ACTIVITY_* variants). Supports both relative and absolute date ranges, plus a rich set of filters (teams, users, call direction/outcome, tags, AI Voice Agent interventions, and more). Retrieve an Analytics Report Export â Poll an export job. When the job completes, the response includes a presigned, time-limited downloadUrl . Requires the Analytics+ entitlement. 20-05-2026 Create an Analytics Report Export Retrieve an Analytics Report Export N/A New WhatsApp Message Endpoints Four new endpoints are available for WhatsApp messaging via the public API: Send WhatsApp Message in Agent Conversation â Send a WhatsApp message that is stored in the agent conversation and visible to agents in their Aircall apps. Send WhatsApp Message Skipping Aircall Inbox â Send a WhatsApp message (text, media, or template) from a WhatsApp-capable number without storing it in the Aircall inbox. Designed for high-volume or automated use cases. List WhatsApp Templates â Retrieve a paginated list of WhatsApp templates associated with a WhatsApp-capable number. Get WhatsApp Line Status â Retrieve the current WhatsApp registration and health status of a WhatsApp-capable number. 15-05-2026 Send WhatsApp Message in Agent Conversation Send WhatsApp Message Skipping Aircall Inbox List WhatsApp Templates Get WhatsApp Line Status N/A Trigger an Outbound Call endpoint A new endpoint is available to programmatically place outbound calls from an Outbound Voice Agent . External systems can trigger AI Voice Agent outbound calls for appointment reminders, billing follow-ups, surveys, lead qualification and similar workflows. The agent must be configured in the Aircall Dashboard with a phone number and first message before the endpoint can be used. 14-05-2026 Trigger an Outbound Call N/A Mobile URL Schemes The Aircall mobile apps now support the aircall:// URL scheme, allowing third-party applications to initiate calls directly within the Aircall app by pre-filling the dialpad. Call (Android & iOS) â Available since Android v8.2.0 and iOS v9.9.0 27-03-2026 Call (Android & iOS) N/A Send Group Message endpoints Two new endpoints are available for group messages: Send Group Message â Send a group message from a public API configured number (text or media, one or the other per request). Send Group Message in agent conversation â Send a group text message that is stored in the group conversation and visible to agents in their Aircall apps. 10-03-2026 Send Group Message Send Group Message in agent conversa